#!/usr/bin/env bash
# KratosOS security helpers for tools that aren't packaged in Debian.
set -uo pipefail
case "${1:-help}" in
  install-metasploit)
    # KratosOS will NOT pipe a mutable Internet script into root for you — that
    # is a supply-chain root-execution risk (the upstream branch can change or be
    # compromised between review and run). We give you the official instructions
    # so you can review and pin a release yourself.
    cat <<'TXT'
Metasploit Framework is not in Debian's repositories, so KratosOS does not ship
it. KratosOS deliberately does NOT download and run Rapid7's installer for you,
because that executes mutable Internet code as root.

To install it safely yourself, prefer one of:

  1. A pinned release + checksum (recommended):
       - Open https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/releases
       - Download the release and its published checksum/signature.
       - Verify the checksum, THEN install.

  2. Rapid7's APT repository (review before trusting):
       - Instructions: https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework#installing
       - Read their 'msfinstall' script first; pin the exact commit you reviewed
         (https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-omnibus at a fixed SHA), verify a
         separately obtained digest, and only then run it.

Free, already-installed alternatives for a lot of Metasploit's use cases live in
the "KratosOS Security" menu (searchsploit, hydra, nmap NSE, sqlmap, ...).
TXT
    ;;
  *)
    echo "usage: kratos-sec install-metasploit" ;;
esac
